Behavior contract

Same Source + same ExternalID = one logical item.

Different Source + same ExternalID = different items.

Within one ingestion batch, first occurrence wins.

Across replays, database upsert preserves one durable row.

Concurrent ingestion cannot create duplicate identities because uniqueness is enforced by PostgreSQL.

A retry is a transport concern; deduplication is a data-integrity concern. They remain separate layers.